{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1551579-fog-of-eternity","id":1551579,"title":"Fog of Eternity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-06-10T20:33:08-07:00","id":1551579,"title":"Fog of Eternity","content":"So, I'm thinking of running a past-game in which the characters play their mortal-lives to their embrace; however, the back-story they have in modern-times won't be even close to their actual mortal-lives; I got this idea from Interview with the Vampire, show, in which Louie couldn't remember if it was raining on a particular-day. <br /> <br /> Does anyone else use Fog of Eternity in this way?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-10T20:47:53-07:00","id":1551580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1551579-fog-of-eternity#post1551579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm thinking of running a past-game in which the characters play their mortal-lives to their embrace; however, the back-story they have in modern-times won't be even close to their actual mortal-lives; I got this idea from Interview with the Vampire, show, in which Louie couldn't remember if it was raining on a particular-day.<br /> <br /> Does anyone else use Fog of Eternity in this way?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mess with it in a number of ways. Sometimes a vampire won't be certain of details of a particular day in its mortal years or one of its early nights, others they will remember vividly things so bizarre &amp; absurd that one might question the reality of a memory if there are no witnesses to confirm and so on. And then there are things that blur the lines hard, like glimpses of the final death of a sire, childe or regnant at a time one was supposedly on torpor (blood sympathy at work, memories twisted by dominate, both, neither?) and more.<br /> <br /> But then i've stolen a bunch of elements and mechanic bits from how Oneiros works in <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Astral_Realms\" target=\"_blank\">Astral Realms</a> (mixed with some <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/World_of_Darkness:_Book_of_the_Dead\" target=\"_blank\">Book of Dead</a>) to expand on ideas and concepts in the Sleep of Ages &amp; Torpor from Mythologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-10-2025, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}